# --- compose (the local stack, twelve files) --------------------------------
#
# Measured: 7 partially adopted, 2 absent, 0 current. The packet's "differs by
# ~450 lines" is confirmed and is the smallest of the numbers here — the
# headline is not the size of the diff, it is that NOT ONE service has the
# stack.
#
# The measurement that matters: of the twelve files kit ships, the fleet holds
# `docker-compose.yml` in SIX services and `.env.example` in two, and seven
# services hold at least one member of the twelve (`pantry` holds
# `.env.example` and no compose file, which is why it reads as partially
# adopted rather than absent). The collector, the three trace/metric stores and
# the Grafana provisioning are **0 for 12 across all nine services**. The
# reporter says "partially adopted" rather than reporting eleven separate cells
# and calling the seven successes adoption.
#
# WHAT THESE ARE, AND IT IS NOT "A BROKEN STACK". Checked, because the first
# draft of this file said "so it cannot start" and that was a guess dressed as a
# measurement:
#
#   $ grep -cE '\./(otel-collector|tempo|loki|grafana)' */docker-compose.yml
#   billing 0  courier 0  darkroom 0  gateway 0  identity 0  muse 0
#   $ grep -cE '^\s+- \./' templates/compose/docker-compose.yml
#   5
#
# None of the six mounts a single one of kit's stack files. They declare ONE OR
# TWO SERVICES of their own (`db`, `postgres`, `gateway`, `identity`, `muse`,
# `darkroom`) and they are not kit's stack with pieces removed — they are
# REPLACEMENTS that kept a filename. `docker compose config` is GREEN on five of
# the six, so they are valid, runnable stacks. They are simply not this one.
#
# The five bind mounts are worth being exact about, because an earlier draft of
# this file said the compose file "mounts the other eleven files by path". It
# binds FOUR paths, and one of them is a directory: `./otel-collector.yml`,
# `./tempo/tempo.yaml`, `./loki/loki-config.yaml` and
# `./grafana/provisioning` — the last of which holds five of the bundle's
# members. That is every non-compose member except `.env.example`, which is not
# mounted at all: it is `cp`'d to `.env`, which is why it is a bundle member at
# all.
#
# So the honest reason is the boring one: these seven predate kit's
# observability profile, nobody re-copied, and nobody recorded a decision. That
# is a backlog entry, which is what this file is for.
#
# ONE REAL DEFECT THE BYTE-COMPARISON CANNOT SEE, recorded here because the
